commit 17c7b06cd19ae9e709f62ae5b0cf922697c29eb2
Author: Buu <buddingnewinsights@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 25 11:51:51 2026 +0700

    feat(helper): interpolate setAnimation on the Rust side (S12a+b)
    
    Runtime per-element animation state (starts, target, start instant,
    duration, easing) captured at APPLY time — before the mutation merges the
    targets into the static style, and from the in-flight interpolated value
    when retargeting (S12b: no jump). Render substitutes the interpolated
    number for touched keys in every build loop (div/input/textarea + list
    wrapper + list items share the frame-start clock snapshot), requests the
    next animation frame while any transition runs, and drops entries when
    complete, when the element is gone, or under reduce-motion (jump to end;
    the static style already rests at the target — no protocol traffic needed
    to finish).
    
    - ease(): cubic linear/easeIn/easeOut/easeInOut, endpoint + monotonicity
      + midpoint-shape unit tested; interpolation clamps past the end.
    - resolve_start(): retarget continuity unit tested (halfway 200->300
      retarget starts at 250, not the merged 300).
    - Window test window_mode_animation_frames_flow_and_settle: getStats frame
      counts climb during a 400ms transition (>= +3 frames) and settle after
      (<= +1 frame over 300ms). Observed RED with the RAF call disabled
      (5 -> 6 frames = no loop), then GREEN.
    
    cargo 91/91 (window suite 10/10), bun 79/79, tsc x3, clippy -D warnings,
    fmt clean.

